    "peer_reviewed": "Proceedings of the 34th ACM International Conference on Multimedia (MM ’26), as stated in the paper",
    "problems": "The study does not analyze individual neuron responses or test whether their mixed responses share a feature. The authors note that CLIP is not necessarily a neutral similarity judge; fixed-position temporal pairing is vulnerable to camera motion; only two backbones and two datasets are used; and k=64 and 8× expansion are fixed.",
    "rows_left_out": "No additional results on SAE reconstruction, temporal coherence, action probes, targeted ablation, or retrieval are included because they do not measure neuron polysemanticity or the related SAE-feature MonoSemanticity metric.",
